# Where the match API answers in production. Committed on purpose, like `.env.development`: it is a
# public URL, not a secret.
#
# THIS IS BAKED INTO THE BUNDLE. Vite replaces `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL` with a string literal at
# build time, so this is not configuration the deployed site reads — it is a value compiled into the
# JavaScript. Changing the API's address means rebuilding and redeploying, and it is why this lives in
# the repo rather than in the Pages dashboard: a value compiled into the artifact should be versioned
# with the code that compiled it.
#
# Vite loads `.env.development` ONLY in dev mode, so without this file a production build gets
# `undefined`, falls back to the empty string in `screens/mp/Friendly.tsx`, and calls its own origin.
# That failure is worse than a 404: `public/_redirects` sends `/*` to `index.html` with status 200, so
# an API call gets the HTML page back and the error surfaces as JSON parsing choking on `<`.
VITE_API_URL=https://fut-api.gfoliver.workers.dev
